Build libpcap.so on QNX: configure only knows how to build a shared library on the systems it lists, so QNX got the static archive alone. QNX uses GCC and GNU ld conventions (-shared, -fpic, -Wl,-soname), same as Linux and the BSDs. ctypes users (scapy) need the shared object.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -4782,7 +4782,7 @@
 	    aix*)
 		    ;;
 
-	    freebsd*|netbsd*|openbsd*|dragonfly*|linux*|osf*|haiku*|midipix*)
+	    freebsd*|netbsd*|openbsd*|dragonfly*|linux*|osf*|haiku*|midipix*|nto-qnx*)
 		    #
 		    # Platforms where the C compiler is GCC or accepts
 		    # compatible command-line arguments, and the linker
@@ -10120,7 +10120,7 @@
 	MAN_MISC_INFO=5
 	;;
 
-linux*|freebsd*|netbsd*|openbsd*|dragonfly*|kfreebsd*|gnu*|haiku*|midipix*)
+linux*|freebsd*|netbsd*|openbsd*|dragonfly*|kfreebsd*|gnu*|haiku*|midipix*|nto-qnx*)
 	DYEXT="so"
 	;;
 
